---
const rules = [
  'One rule or fact per line.',
  'The reason in one clause, or the person\'s own words quoted exactly.',
  'Rules say what to do.',
  'Condition first, then the instruction.',
  'At most 20 words per instruction.',
  'Active voice.',
  'Every fact dated.',
];
---

<section class="border-b border-border/40">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-6 py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.22em] text-muted mb-6">
      05 · How the files are written
    </p>
    <h2 class="font-display text-3xl sm:text-4xl text-ink tracking-tight mb-8">
      Rules from aircraft maintenance manuals.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-ink-dim leading-relaxed max-w-2xl mb-10">
      The writing rules come from ASD&#8209;STE100 Simplified Technical
      English, the controlled language of aircraft maintenance manuals.
      Every line in the portrait and the landscapes follows them.
    </p>

    <ol class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      {
        rules.map((r, i) => (
          <li class="rounded-md border border-border/60 bg-bg/40 px-5 py-4 text-sm text-ink-dim leading-relaxed">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-accent mr-2">{i + 1}</span>
            {r}
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ol>

    <p class="mt-10 text-sm text-ink-dim italic max-w-2xl">
      A system for how to build a sentence works better than a list of words
      to avoid.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
